Source: tolome-locales
Section: localization
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Anhky <dev@tolome.net>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: tolome-locales
Architecture: all
Depends: locales, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Locales of Tolome (French of Benin fr_BJ, Fon fon_BJ)
 Adds locales that glibc does not provide: fr_BJ (French, Benin: CFA franc
 "25 000 F CFA", comma decimal point, narrow no-break space for thousands,
 +229 telephone code) and fon_BJ (Fon, Benin: Fon day and month names, yes/no
 words, 31-letter alphabet for sorting). The definitions are compiled with
 localedef at installation and when the locales package is upgraded, into
 /usr/lib/locale (no locale-archive, no file of glibc or locales modified).
 .
 /usr/share/i18n/SUPPORTED is diverted (dpkg-divert) and regenerated by a
 trigger so that installers such as Calamares list the new locales. The
 default language is not changed. Removing the package removes the compiled
 locales and gives SUPPORTED back to locales.
